title: Example - Marker as procedure call
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Default,demo

A v1.0 marker can call a `\procedure` and bake several static parameters into the call. The marker body fills the one dynamic parameter named by `src-name`.

Both markers below share the same `.greet` procedure but bake different parameters. They use the modern `<$transclude $variable="..." $mode="block" ...>` widget (TW 5.3+, see [[TranscludeWidget|https://tiddlywiki.com/#TranscludeWidget]]).

><<.tid-source text:"""HELLO This is the body for HELLO.
---

GREETING This is the body for GREETING.
---""">>

!! The two markers

